YOUR TASK: Complete this task: Implement the complete Python solution using the fixed baseline parity-correction algorithm: for each test case choose p_i as any maximizing attribute (e.g. first max), compute M_i, sort by M_i descending, take the top 2K cakes as S, and compute baseline sum B and parity mask T (xor of 1<<p_i). If T=0 output B. Otherwise build top-two structures: selected cakes by smallest M_i for each base label; unselected cakes by largest value for each label; for each selected cake, recolor operations to other labels (cost M_i - value_i(b), mask (1<<p_i)^(1<<b)) keeping top two distinct selected ids per mask; swap operations for each b != p_i with cost M_i - best_unselected_value[b] for the same mask, keeping top two distinct selected ids per mask. Compute min loss as the best single operation of mask T, or the best conflict-free pair of operations with the other two masks: recolor+recolor and recolor+swap via top-two distinct selected ids; swap+swap by enumerating the two ordered (source,target) label pairs for each mask, taking the minimum distinct selected M sum (top two if same source label) and maximum distinct unselected value sum (top two if same target label, checking ids). Output B - min loss. Use Python ints, handle no unselected when K=N/2, and ensure the sample outputs are produced.